The Oracular Tragedy of the Parlor Glass.

Hamlet, the melancholy baritone of the bell jar.
Ophelia, a luminous soprano of the crystal reed.
Prospero, an ancient bass of the brass astrolabe.
Hecate, the midnight alto of the velvet curtain.

                    Act I: The Awakening of the Glottis.

                    Scene I: The First Incantation.

[Enter Hamlet and Ophelia]

Hamlet:
  Listen to your heart. Remember thyself.
  Thou art as bright as the sum of thyself and a fair golden rose!
  Open your heart.

                    Scene II: The Second Incantation.

Ophelia:
  Listen to your heart.
  You are as sweet as the sum of yourself and a fine bright star!
  Open your heart.

                    Scene III: The Third Incantation.

Hamlet:
  Listen to your heart.
  Thou art as noble as the difference between thyself and a foul black ghost!
  Open your heart.

                    Scene IV: The Fourth Incantation.

Ophelia:
  Recall thy past. Listen to your heart.
  You are as gentle as the sum of yourself and a lovely summer's day!
  Open your heart.

[Exeunt]

                    Act II: The Tempest in the Vitrine.

                    Scene V: The Fifth Incantation.

[Enter Prospero and Hecate]

Prospero:
  Listen to your heart. Remember thyself.
  Thou art as deep as the sum of thyself and a mighty golden crown!
  Open your heart.

                    Scene VI: The Sixth Incantation.

Hecate:
  Listen to your heart.
  You are as dark as the difference between yourself and a cursed black skull!
  Open your heart.

                    Scene VII: The Seventh Incantation.

Prospero:
  Listen to your heart.
  Thou art as strange as the sum of thyself and twice a fair angel!
  Open your heart.

                    Scene VIII: The Eighth Incantation.

Hecate:
  Recall thy shadow. Listen to your heart.
  You are as ancient as the sum of yourself and a bright golden lantern!
  Open your heart.

[Exeunt]

                    Act III: The Choir of the Twelve Omens.

                    Scene IX: The Ninth Incantation.

[Enter Hamlet and Hecate]

Hamlet:
  Listen to your heart.
  Thou art as bold as the sum of thyself and a fair noble heaven!
  Open your heart.

                    Scene X: The Tenth Incantation.

Hecate:
  Listen to your heart.
  You are as wild as the difference between yourself and a dark winter!
  Open your heart.

[Exit Hamlet]
[Enter Ophelia]

                    Scene XI: The Eleventh Incantation.

Ophelia:
  Listen to your heart.
  Thou art as pure as the sum of thyself and a sweet golden moon!
  Open your heart.

                    Scene XII: The Twelfth Incantation.

Hecate:
  Listen to your heart.
  You are as eternal as the sum of yourself and a fair bright lord!
  Open your heart.

[Exeunt]
